cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it. A DOI will be added here once the first release is archived on Zenodo."
title: "Catkin Biofilm Adsorption: physics-informed modelling of reactive dye adsorption on a Saccharum spontaneum (Catkin) flower-fibre CMC/PVA/TiO2 biofilm"
abstract: >-
  Code accompanying a study of Avitera Light Red SE adsorption on a
  citric-acid crosslinked PVA/TiO2/cellulose-microcrystal (CMC) biofilm, in
  which the CMC was extracted from Saccharum spontaneum (Catkin) flower
  fibre. Includes classical pseudo-first/second-order kinetics and
  Langmuir/Freundlich isotherm fitting, and PINN3D, a physics-informed
  neural network that jointly fits the kinetics and isotherm data through a
  shared mass-balance constraint to estimate adsorption performance under
  contact time, concentration and dosage combinations that were not
  directly measured, with leave-one-out cross-validation reported alongside
  the in-sample fit.
type: software
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
